2,"_146":173,"_131":174},{"_142":143,"_117":130,"_119":168,"_146":169,"_131":170},"Illustrative examples stay labelled as illustrative. They are used to explain a workflow, not to imply a completed client result.",[171],"[data-approved-section=\"1-paragraph-2\"]",{"_142":119,"_152":168},"No team scale, client roster, performance figure, award, testimonial or guarantee is published as fact until the source, permission and approval record exist.",[175],"[data-approved-section=\"1-paragraph-1\"]",{"_142":119,"_152":172},"What is not published as proof","[data-approved-section=\"1-heading\"]","[data-approved-section=\"0\"]",[160],{"_157":130,"_119":193},[182,183,184],{"_142":136,"_117":118,"_157":130,"_119":193,"_131":194},{"_142":143,"_117":144,"_119":189,"_146":190,"_131":191},{"_142":143,"_117":130,"_119":185,"_146":186,"_131":187},"The objective is to make websites, apps and AI-assisted systems easier to understand, easier to operate and easier to hand over.",[188],"[data-approved-section=\"0-paragraph-2\"]",{"_142":119,"_152":185},"The work starts with a named problem, an accountable owner and a defined first release. Technology choices follow the workflow, not the other way around.",[192],"[data-approved-section=\"0-paragraph-1\"]",{"_142":119,"_152":189},"How Silverstone approaches delivery","[data-approved-section=\"0-heading\"]",{"_117":118,"_157":144,"_119":33},{"_117":144,"_157":130,"_119":193},{"_117":130,"_157":130,"_119":193},{"_117":205,"_157":130,"_119":176},{"_117":204,"_157":130,"_119":176},{"_117":203,"_157":130,"_119":158},{"_117":202,"_157":130,"_119":158},6,5,4,3,{"_117":118,"_207":208,"_209":210,"_211":212},"types",[78,79,80],"rawJson","{\n  \"approvedRoute\": \"/about\",\n  \"description\": \"Learn how Silverstone approaches websites, apps and AI workflows for UK businesses, with clear scope, human oversight and evidence-led delivery.\",\n  \"name\": \"About Silverstone AI | Practical Digital Systems\",\n  \"note\": \"Approved editorial overlay f